From e53f1a78baf4fd5a016ee7a1a37e87ace3ead317 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 16:43:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/21] fix(steam): give the x86-64 client's windows an OpenGL
 that works here, and stop endless web helper restarts

A Snapdragon 685's logs (0.7.1-sd685.3): Steam's composer in steamwebhelper logged "CreateOutputWindow:
failed to acquire a gl context", fell back to the system composer, and the client restarted its web helper
23 times, about every 45 s, with no window ever reaching gamescope. FEX's thunked GL failed underneath
("failed to create dri3 screen", "failed to load driver: zink"). The CEF GPU process never crashed, so the
0.7.1-sd685.3 watch had nothing to see, and it had died anyway: under the launcher's set -e its first grep
that found nothing ended it silently.

- x64_gl_try / x64_gl_mode: before the client starts, x86 glxinfo -B through FEX on the session's display,
  through the thunks and then with the rootfs's llvmpipe. Only a mode that printed a renderer is used
  (glxinfo exits 0 on failure too). Kept per FEX build, rootfs and driver variables; nothing is decided or
  kept when it cannot be checked.
- x64_first_frame_watch: set +e; counts composer GL failures (webhelper.txt), web helper restarts
  (steamui_html.txt) and Chromium GPU exits from this start on (a rotated log from its start). On the GPU
  path one composer failure or two restarts move the client to software OpenGL once per session, only
  when a software context works; four restarts stop the client instead of looping. Progress lines name
  the restarts and the OpenGL in use.
- The repair after two starts without an image no longer downloads the client again when the watch saw
  an OpenGL cause ("cause opengl"); a requested repair also forgets the OpenGL answer.
- LoadingState + strings (en, es, es-419): the new steps are explained on the loading screen.
- Tests run under set -eu with the phone's log lines, a FEX stand-in and an x86 glxinfo stand-in.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
