diff --git a/docs/development/x86-64-steam-client.md b/docs/development/x86-64-steam-client.md
index cf25613..5334b1d 100644
--- a/docs/development/x86-64-steam-client.md
+++ b/docs/development/x86-64-steam-client.md
@@ -234,6 +234,26 @@ alone would then read as an installed client.
   web helper's GPU process keeps exiting until Chromium gives up on the GPU (the menus then never appear),
   one line says so with the exit codes, followed by x86 `glxinfo -B` and `vulkaninfo --summary` through
   FEX's thunks.
+- **OpenGL for the client's own windows** (`x64_gl_mode`). Steam draws its menus with its own composer
+  inside steamwebhelper (`CCompositorGLThread`), which needs an OpenGL context whatever the CEF flags say.
+  Without one it logs `CreateOutputWindow: failed to acquire a gl context`, falls back to the system composer
+  and the client restarts the helper (`Restart webhelper process`) about every 45 s for ever: a Snapdragon
+  685 (Adreno 610, KGSL) did that 23 times, FEX's thunked GL failing with `failed to create dri3 screen` /
+  `failed to load driver: zink`. So before the client starts, x86 `glxinfo -B` through FEX is run on the
+  session's display, first through the thunks, then with the rootfs's own llvmpipe
+  (`LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE=1`); a mode counts only when glxinfo printed a renderer (it exits 0 on failure
+  too). The answer is kept in `~/.droiddeck-x64/.droiddeck-gl-mode`, keyed by the FEX build, the rootfs and
+  the driver variables; `software` starts the client with the x64_env software branch and `-cef-disable-gpu`.
+  Nothing is decided or kept when it cannot be checked (no glxinfo, no display). `BL_X64_GL_PROBE=0` skips it.
+- **First-frame watch** (`x64_first_frame_watch`, until the app writes `~/.bl-first-frame`). It runs with
+  `set +e` (0.7.1-sd685.3's ended silently under the launcher's `set -e`) and counts, from the lines each
+  log had when the client started (or from the start of a log Steam rotated), composer GL failures
+  (`webhelper.txt`), helper restarts (`steamui_html.txt`) and Chromium GPU exits (`console-linux.txt`). On
+  the GPU path, one composer failure or two restarts move the client to software OpenGL once per session,
+  only when a software context works (`.bl-restart-software`, restarted by droiddeck-session). Four restarts
+  (`BL_X64_WATCH_RESTARTS`) stop the client instead of looping. It writes `cause opengl` into
+  `package/droiddeck-unconfirmed`, so the two-starts-without-an-image repair does not download the
+  client's files again for a problem they do not have. A requested repair also forgets the OpenGL answer.
 
 ## DroidDeck direct for Linux games and runtimes
 
